# Dependencies are installed by Vercel on every build. Committing them is what
# broke the deployments before, so they stay out of the repo permanently.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Local env files. Vercel holds the real values as project environment
# variables; nothing secret belongs in the repo.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Build caches
.vercel/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Astro's generated folder.
#
# The TYPE DECLARATIONS inside it are tracked on purpose. They are what lets a
# fresh clone typecheck before anyone has run `astro sync`, and a change to them
# is a real change worth seeing in a diff — previously the whole folder was
# ignored while every file in it was already tracked, so `types.d.ts` sat
# permanently modified and could not be committed without -f.
#
# Only the machine-local caches beside them stay out. `settings.json` holds
# nothing but an update-check timestamp, so tracking it would put a meaningless
# one-line diff in every commit and bury the changes this rule exists to show.
#
# The pattern ignores the folder's CONTENTS (`/*`) rather than the folder
# itself: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so
# `**/.astro/` with a `!` negation below it would silently do nothing.
**/.astro/*
!**/.astro/*.d.ts
!**/.astro/*.mjs

# Vendored design skills, installed by a command rather than committed — the
# same rule node_modules follows above.
#
#   npx impeccable install          -> .claude/skills/impeccable, .github/*
#   npx skills@latest add emilkowalski/skills  -> .agents/skills + symlinks
#
# `.agents/skills/` IS tracked: it is 150KB of real files and the actual source
# for the Emil skills. What is ignored is everything derived from it or
# reinstallable:
#
#  - `.claude/skills/<emil skill>` are ABSOLUTE symlinks into one machine's home
#    directory. Committing them hands every other clone a broken path.
#  - `.github/skills` and `.github/hooks` are a byte-identical 3.2MB copy of
#    impeccable for GitHub Copilot, which nothing in this project uses.
#  - `.claude/skills/impeccable` is 3.2MB restored by one command.
#
# The Itqan skills under `.claude/skills/itqan-*` are OURS and stay tracked.
.claude/skills/impeccable/
.claude/skills/animation-vocabulary
.claude/skills/apple-design
.claude/skills/emil-design-eng
.claude/skills/find-animation-opportunities
.claude/skills/improve-animations
.claude/skills/pick-ui-library
.claude/skills/prototype
.claude/skills/review-animations
.github/skills/
.github/hooks/

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
